†[÷â®bCxí®-çt{"rendered":{"html":"<p>GCSL tooling shares language analysis while keeping disk access and editor\nprotocol handling outside the core. This prevents checking and formatting\nfrom depending on an evaluator run.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tooling-state--source-discovery\"><span class=\"heading-number\">300.1</span> Source discovery <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#tooling-state--source-discovery\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p><code>gcsl-disk</code> finds workspace markers and returns a source collection with\nstable path and diagnostic mappings. It excludes hidden names and nested\nworkspace trees when reading one workspace. The CLI and language server\nuse this shared layer rather than implementing separate import rules.</p>\n<p>A check of a directory discovers workspaces. A format of a directory\nfinds source files, including standalone files. Their traversal results\nare therefore intentionally different.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tooling-state--editor-snapshots\"><span class=\"heading-number\">300.2</span> Editor snapshots <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#tooling-state--editor-snapshots\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p><code>gcsl-lsp</code> overlays open document text on disk sources and asks a worker to\ncheck the affected workspace. Queries use an up-to-date semantic index;\nthey can force a pending check before answering. Diagnostics continue to\nrefer to actual source even when a query temporarily repairs unmatched\nbraces to find usable names.</p>\n<p>Rename computes proposed edits and checks their effect before offering\nthem. Standard-library, file, and directory identities are not editable\nthrough that operation. Formatting returns edits from the language's\nformatter rather than applying the editor's formatting preferences.</p>\n<p>Only local <code>file:</code> document URIs with an empty or <code>localhost</code> authority\nand an absolute decoded path map to disk files. Other URI forms are\nchecked as standalone documents, not treated as local workspace paths.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tooling-state--formatter\"><span class=\"heading-number\">300.3</span> Formatter <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#tooling-state--formatter\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The formatter works from tokens, comments, and parsed structure. It does\nnot need evaluation or successful type inference. Syntax errors prevent a\nrewrite of that file. The CLI uses a temporary file and replacement so\nreaders don't observe a partially written formatted file.</p>\n<p>The principal code is in <code>crates/gcsl-disk/src/lib.rs</code>,\n<code>crates/gcsl-lsp/src/</code>, <code>crates/gcsl/src/index/</code>, and\n<code>crates/gcsl/src/fmt.rs</code>. The CLI adapters live in\n<code>crates/gcsl-cli/src/</code>.</p>\n","toc":[{"level":2,"id":"tooling-state--source-discovery","title":"Source discovery","number":"300.1"},{"level":2,"id":"tooling-state--editor-snapshots","title":"Editor snapshots","number":"300.2"},{"level":2,"id":"tooling-state--formatter","title":"Formatter","number":"300.3"}],"has_mermaid":false,"dangling":[],"warnings":[],"broken":[]},"images":[],"links":{"pages":[],"anchors":[]},"refs":null}